SUPERVISOR FINDING (round 2): an origin-inclusion mutant SURVIVED your gate. Forcing coneAffectedCells to pass null instead of `template.includeOrigin ? null : origin` (origin ALWAYS included) leaves the whole templates suite green. Per SRD 5.2.1 a Cone/Cube/Line/Sphere point of origin is NOT in the area unless its creator decides; under the touch-any-part product rule the origin intersection point decides the squares that touch the area ONLY at that point (e.g. the four apex-adjacent squares of a cone), so includeOrigin has observable cell-set consequences that nothing pins. FIX: for EVERY optional-origin shape, add fixtures + named tests that assert the affected-cell set BOTH with includeOrigin false (apex-only-touch squares excluded) and true (included), with hand-derived expectations documented. If your current polygon/exclusion implementation makes includeOrigin a no-op on the cell set, that is a BUG against the product rule — fix the geometry so the flag has its ruled effect, and say so in the report. Re-run afterwards: my mutant (null in place of the conditional) must be killed by a NAMED test per shape; your ledger mutations 27-30 + your two own controls still killed; tests/unit/combat green; tsc both configs. All original rules stand: no git, no full suite, hand-derived expectations only. TERSE final: per-shape origin semantics proof, named killing tests, ledger status.
